            <ArticleTitle>Is media information that smoking causes illness a self-fulfilling prophecy?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>177-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Of 528 men, those 72 who derived information from the media, showed a lower rate of survival, i.e., more deaths from cancer, coronary heart disease, etc. Stress increased by constant repetition of evil consequences of smoking might constitute a self-fulfilling prophecy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
